## Story Description
Add the 12 new analytics fields to the Python-side schema (CanonicalTransaction Pydantic model and SQLAlchemy transactions_table). Populate categorisation_status automatically in the categorisation pipeline (CATEGORISED / UNCATEGORISED based on confidence >= 0.60). Populate abc_segment in the cube pipeline. All new fields are Optional with None defaults so existing tests are unaffected. Update CLAUDE.md with the analytics foundation documentation.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/models/schema.py — add to CanonicalTransaction (all Optional with default None unless noted): legal_entity: Optional[str] = None; vendor_country: Optional[str] = None; plant_country: Optional[str] = None; categorisation_status: Optional[str] = 'uncategorised'; manual_override_flag: Optional[int] = 0; ai_classification_flag: Optional[int] = 0; harmonised_payment_term: Optional[str] = None; discount_percent: Optional[float] = 0.0; discount_days: Optional[int] = 0; has_early_payment_discount: Optional[int] = 0; payment_term_confidence: Optional[float] = None; abc_segment: Optional[str] = None
- Edit file: src/models/database.py — add 12 new columns to transactions_table at the END of the column list (after the existing raw_data column): Column('legal_entity', Text, nullable=True), Column('vendor_country', Text, nullable=True), Column('plant_country', Text, nullable=True), Column('categorisation_status', Text, nullable=True), Column('manual_override_flag', Integer, nullable=True), Column('ai_classification_flag', Integer, nullable=True), Column('harmonised_payment_term', Text, nullable=True), Column('discount_percent', Float, nullable=True), Column('discount_days', Integer, nullable=True), Column('has_early_payment_discount', Integer, nullable=True), Column('payment_term_confidence', Float, nullable=True), Column('abc_segment', Text, nullable=True)
- Edit file: src/categorisation/categoriser.py — after the 6-pass pipeline completes for each transaction, set categorisation_status = 'categorised' if category_confidence >= 0.60 else 'uncategorised'. Also set ai_classification_flag = 1 if category_method == 'LLM' else 0; manual_override_flag = 1 if category_method == 'MANUAL' else 0. This update should happen in the existing result-writing logic.
- Edit file: src/cube/pipeline.py — add an ABC segment computation step after the supplier aggregation step. Compute abc_segment per supplier per engagement using the Pareto convention (A: top 80% of spend, B: next 15%, C: bottom 5%) based on cumulative SUM(base_amount). Write abc_segment back to the transactions table for each transaction belonging to that supplier via UPDATE transactions SET abc_segment = ? WHERE canonical_supplier_id = ? AND engagement_id = ?.
- Verify: pytest tests/ -v --tb=short — all tests pass (new fields are nullable/have defaults, so existing test fixtures are unaffected). Report exact pass/fail count.
- Edit file: CLAUDE.md — append a new section '## Analytics Foundation' documenting: the 12 new transaction fields and their purpose; the three new reference tables (categories, legal_entities, payment_term_mappings); the five new cube endpoints; the FilterContext architecture; the aggregations.ts utility functions; the DrilldownState pattern; and the ABC segmentation convention (A=top 80%, B=next 15%, C=bottom 5%).

